lesson: 207
title: Fingers and toes
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: A person has 2 hands with 5 fingers each, so 10 fingers, and 2 feet with 5 toes each, so 10 toes.
explain: Fingers and toes together make 10 + 10 = 20 for every person.
explain: 3 children have 3 × 20 = 60 fingers and toes. If one of them wears a glove on one hand, the fingers are still there.
vars: a=name b=name p=3..12
answer: 20 * p
exercise: {p} children paddle in the sea. How many fingers and toes do they have altogether?
exercise: {a} and {p-1} friends paint with their fingers and toes. How many fingers and toes are there in the group?
exercise: How many fingers and toes do {p} people have together?
exercise: A family of {p} sits on the beach. How many fingers and toes does the family have?
exercise: {a} counts the fingers and toes of the {p} babies at the nursery. What number does {a.he} get?
exercise: {p} of us at the pool, how many fingers n toes
exercise: {a}'s whole family is {p+1}, sorry {p}, people. fingers + toes?
exercise: {p} kids, barefoot on the grass, it was well hot. fingers and toes all together?
exercise: {b} says {p} people have {10*p} fingers and toes. nah. how many really
exercise: count fingers n toes for {p} people, my maths teacher asked lol
exercise: {p} people in the yoga class, the room was freezing btw. how many fingers and toes
test: Find the total number of fingers and toes on {p} people.
test: Fingers plus toes: how many are there on a team of {p} swimmers?
test: {b} takes off {b.his} socks, and so do {p-1} other children. How many toes and fingers do the {p} children have in all?
test: The {p} people in the lift have how many fingers and toes between them?
test: fingers n toes on {p} ppl?
test: theres {p} of us in the tent. fingers and toes total
exam: Determine the aggregate number of fingers and toes possessed by {p.words} persons.
exam: It is given that a family comprises {p} members. Ascertain the total quantity of digits, fingers and toes alike, belonging to the family.
exam: A class of {p} pupils is assembled. Compute the combined number of fingers and toes pertaining to all pupils so assembled.
exam: Whereas {p} swimmers stand upon the edge of a pool, state the cardinality of the set of their fingers and toes.
exercise: {p+1} children were going to paddle in the sea, but one was 'under the weather' and stayed on the sand. How many fingers and toes are in the water?
exercise: Grandma, who is no spring chicken, watches from her chair while {a} and {p-1} friends paint with their fingers and toes. How many fingers and toes are painting?
test: {p+1} of us at the beach, {b}'s got a tummy bug n is on the loo, rest of us paddling. how many fingers n toes in the water, seriously
